FIX VOLUME-CONV: reconstruct FUN_004165f4 (linear volume -> DirectSound centi-dB)

The assembler emitted a return-0 stub for FUN_004165f4 (no Ghidra body): every
Play_Sound/Modify_Sound SetVolume call got 0 = full volume. The original
@0x4165f4 converts the game's linear 0..0xfff volume, scaled by the master
volume [0x462d84], to DirectSound centi-dB attenuation via
trunc(log10((v+1)/4096)*2768), clamped to [-10000,0] (full derivation incl. the
frndint-chop CRT helper 0x45681c in the code comment). Also gives the CRT
log10 stub @0x45b0cf a real body (via un-stubbed libm log()) and fixes its
forward declaration.

Measured against the sound-enabled wine reference (DS-call capture at the
Play_Sound/Modify_Sound vtable sites, ALSA null device): ref's first race
volumes are -9999 (master volume [0x462d84] still 0) -- the reconstruction
reproduces them exactly; later values depend only on [0x462d84], which evolves
identically (game state is bit-identical).

--- a/dd2.c
+++ b/dd2.c
@@ -843,7 +843,7 @@
 int FUN_0045b06a();
 int IF_DLOG2();
 int IF_DLOG10();
-int log10();
+double log10(double);   /* patch 725: real CRT log10 body @0x45b0cf */
 int log2();
 int floor();
 int _Scale();
@@ -5998,7 +5998,34 @@
 
 
 /* ===== FUN_004165f4 @ 004165f4 ===== */
-int FUN_004165f4(){ return 0; }
+/* Reconstructed from asm (Ghidra didn't export a body; the assembly stub returned 0 -> every
+   sound played at FULL volume). Linear game volume -> DirectSound centi-dB attenuation:
+     0x4165f8  v = abs(arg)                     (cltd; xor; sub)
+     0x416603  if (v > 0xfff) v = 0xfff
+     0x416614  v = v * [0x462d84]master / 0xfff (imul; idiv 0xfff)
+     0x41662a  x87: log10((v+1) * [0x46c84c]=1/4096) * [0x46c854]=2768.0
+               (fildl; fld1; faddp; fmull; fldlg2; fyl2x; fmull)
+     0x416643  call 0x45681c = frndint with CW hi-byte 0x1f (RC=11 chop) = trunc()
+     0x41664b  clamp to [-10000, 0]
+   Ref-verified: with master=0 (image default) every input yields -9999 = the reference's
+   first race SetVolume captures. (int) cast = the chop rounding. Min distance of all 4096
+   possible log10 products to an integer boundary is 6.4e-5, so 1-ulp libm differences
+   (glibc vs musl/wasm) cannot flip the trunc -> result stays bit-identical across targets. */
+int __cdecl FUN_004165f4(int param_1)
+{
+  int iVar1;
+  double dVar2;
+  
+  iVar1 = param_1;
+  if (iVar1 < 0) iVar1 = -iVar1;
+  if (0xfff < iVar1) iVar1 = 0xfff;
+  iVar1 = iVar1 * DAT_00462d84 / 0xfff;
+  dVar2 = log10((double)(iVar1 + 1) * 0.000244140625) * 2768.0;
+  iVar1 = (int)dVar2;
+  if (iVar1 < -10000) iVar1 = -10000;
+  if (0 < iVar1) iVar1 = 0;
+  return iVar1;
+}
 /* ===== CD_Check @ 00416670 ===== */
 
 undefined4 CD_Check(void)
@@ -46890,7 +46917,15 @@
 /* ===== IF_DLOG10 @ 0045b0b8 ===== */
 int IF_DLOG10(){ return 0; }
 /* ===== log10 @ 0045b0cf ===== */
-int log10(){ return 0; }
+/* real CRT log10 (was a return-0 stub; needed by the reconstructed FUN_004165f4). Implemented
+   via the un-stubbed libm log(): log10(x) = log(x)/ln(10). The 1e-16-relative double-rounding
+   difference vs a native log10 is 8 orders of magnitude below the 6.4e-5 integer-boundary
+   margin of the only caller's trunc, so results are identical. */
+double log10(double __x)
+{
+  double log(double);
+  return log(__x) * 0.43429448190325176;
+}
 /* ===== log2 @ 0045b0e2 ===== */
 int log2(){ return 0; }
